From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ai_re <ai_re@localhost>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 30/35] spi: designware: no slave selected while the TX FIFO is
 loaded

The transfer code loads the TX FIFO before it writes SER, and nothing
cleared SER beforehand: a slave select left set by earlier firmware makes
the first command start on a chip that is still selected. On the Alpine V2
DMC-12, started by al-boot stage3 (which reads the boot flash through the
SSI's memory-mapped window and turns the CS override on just before it
jumps), the first RDID then read ff ff ff and the SPI env failed to load;
every later command worked, because each transfer ends with SER = 0.
The Annapurna HAL that the vendor U-Boot uses writes SER = 0 with the SSI
disabled before every transfer (al_spi_read, 0x0112b3f8 there).

Clear SER at hw init and, with the SSI disabled, at the start of every
mem-op transfer. On Alpine, report a select found set at probe.

Scope: alpine-v2 (generic driver code).
---
 drivers/spi/designware_spi.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/designware_spi.c b/drivers/spi/designware_spi.c
index 3e5aefb1..9d7d99a7 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/designware_spi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/designware_spi.c
@@ -218,7 +218,18 @@ static int dw_spi_apb_k210_init(struct udevice *bus, struct dw_spi_priv *priv)
  */
 static int dw_spi_alpine_init(struct udevice *bus, struct dw_spi_priv *priv)
 {
-	int ret = dw_spi_apb_init(bus, priv);
+	u32 ser = dw_read(priv, DW_SPI_SER);
+	int ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * al-boot stage3 reads the boot flash through the SSI's memory-mapped
+	 * window (0xf8000000) and can start its application with SER still
+	 * set; spi_hw_init() clears it. Report it: a select left set made the
+	 * first command after a cold stage3 boot read ff ff ff.
+	 */
+	if (ser)
+		printf("SSI:   slave select %#x left set by the firmware, cleared\n", ser);
+	ret = dw_spi_apb_init(bus, priv);
 
 	if (!ret)
 		dw_write(priv, DW_SPI_CS_OVERRIDE, 0xf);
@@ -284,6 +295,13 @@ static void spi_hw_init(struct udevice *bus, struct dw_spi_priv *priv)
 {
 	dw_write(priv, DW_SPI_SSIENR, 0);
 	dw_write(priv, DW_SPI_IMR, 0);
+	/*
+	 * Deselect every chip. The transfer code loads the TX FIFO before it
+	 * writes SER, so a slave select left set by earlier firmware would
+	 * start the first command on a chip that is still selected, e.g. in
+	 * the middle of a memory-mapped read the boot loader left open.
+	 */
+	dw_write(priv, DW_SPI_SER, 0);
 	dw_write(priv, DW_SPI_SSIENR, 1);
 
 	/*
@@ -628,6 +646,8 @@ static int dw_spi_exec_op(struct spi_slave *slave, const struct spi_mem_op *op)
 		op->data.nbytes);
 
 	dw_write(priv, DW_SPI_SSIENR, 0);
+	/* no chip selected while the FIFO is loaded (the Alpine HAL does this too) */
+	dw_write(priv, DW_SPI_SER, 0);
 	dw_write(priv, DW_SPI_CTRLR0, cr0);
 	if (read)
 		dw_write(priv, DW_SPI_CTRLR1, op->data.nbytes - 1);
